Dawn, Securing the Post
[trigger none]
[vignette dungeons/relay_post]

FIXME(action): Ossal sets his cup down and waits for your lead. The wire ticks once. Devra has noticed something. She is at her desk. She is very still. She is watching you both.

choices:

* Confront her openly = Tell her what is happening and ask her to stand down
    FIXME(action): You cross the room and tell her plainly. Ossal has asked for your help. The post stays open. The copies stay here. You are not going to fight her and you are not going to lie. You are asking her to sit down.
    FIXME(dread): She argues. Passionately, logically, with the specific evidence from her log, line by line, citation by citation. When it is clear you are not changing your mind, she stops. She sits down at her desk. She goes quiet. Ossal goes through her pack. He finds the wax-paper sleeve under her bedroll. He puts it all in his case. The relay stays operational, and you depart. On the way back to the main road, you encounter a pair of Kesharat warriors. They're looking for Ossal. You exchange pleasantries and direct them to the station.
    +finish_dungeon
    +add_level

* Take the copies from her pack = Distract Devra at the desk while Ossal goes for the pack [requires tag relay_post.kept_copies]
    FIXME(action): Devra told you last night the wax-paper sleeve is in her pack. Her pack is on the floor by the leg of her desk, near her feet. You approach the desk on the side away from the pack and open a conversation. The plan is to draw her attention to your side long enough for Ossal to cross from the brazier, crouch on the other side, and lift the sleeve out without her noticing.
    @if check cunning correct:scheme wrong:bluff {
        FIXME(action): You sit down across from her and ask a question about the resonance-platform order: a real question, one she answers carefully because it is the order that frightens her most. Her attention stays on the answer. Ossal crosses behind her, kneels at the pack, finds the wax-paper sleeve under a folded shirt, and lifts it out. He is back at the brazier before she finishes her sentence. When she sees the sleeve in his hand a few minutes later her expression goes flat.
        FIXME(revelation): The originals stay in the file. The copies stay in Ossal's case. The relay stays operational. Devra will keep doing her job. She will do it well. She no longer believes in the work.
        +give_gold 15
        +finish_dungeon
        +add_level
    } @else {
        FIXME(action): You sit down across from her and try to make conversation, but you cannot stop your eyes flicking toward the pack at her feet. She sees it. She is fast. She has the wax-paper sleeve out of the pack and into the brazier coals before Ossal has crossed half the room. You all stand and watch the duplicates blacken and curl. The room smells of burning paper.
        FIXME(dread): The originals are still in the official file. Without her annotation log they read as routine messages with slightly unusual content. The evidence is gone. Ossal sits down heavily. He does not look at you. The relay stays operational. The thing you came here to preserve is destroyed.
        +give_gold 15
        +finish_dungeon
    }

* Search the post on Ossal's hunch = Turn the place over while Ossal holds her at the desk [requires !tag relay_post.kept_copies]
    FIXME(action): You don't know what you are looking for. You search anyway. You go through her pack. You go through the back storeroom. You turn out the supply crates. Ossal cannot operate the wire to confirm anything from the capital, so he cannot even tell you what evidence would prove what. After an hour you have found nothing. Ossal touches your elbow and shakes his head.
    FIXME(dread): Devra has been sitting at her desk this whole time with the look of a woman waiting for two men to finish a tantrum in her workspace. When you stop she goes back to her log. She does not speak to you. She does not speak to Ossal. Ossal cannot bring himself to apologize. He cannot bring himself to release her, either. He stands at the brazier with his hands behind his back, not looking at her, not looking at you.
    +give_gold 15
    +finish_dungeon
